    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for that. To get a bit more specific, some of the analysts on our side are suggesting that this particular kind of multi-ethnic mix in this part of the world is inherently more volatile than, say, a more homogeneous country in Europe or East Asia. They're arguing that \"tribalism\" isn't just a risk, but a predictable outcome whenever you have these specific types of demographic splits. Do you think there's merit to that perspective, or is that just an oversimplification of how these regions operate?",
